(property "Value" "TPS2553DBVR" (at 0 -2.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) ))
(property "Footprint" "Package_TO_SOT_SMD:SOT-23-6" (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
(property "Datasheet" "https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps2553.pdf" (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
(property "Description" " | design | W2 CTRL-6 (W2 CTRL-5 decision, build/15 \"Захист VSYS Pico за D301\"; reviews RV4-E-3, RV4-S-1): constant-current TPS2553DBVR (no -1) ahead of D301, so a short of the Pico VSYS, of C307 or inside the Pico module is limited to IOS 0.154-0.209 A with RILIM R397 150k 1 % (SLVS841G Rev. G, Oct 2026, eq. 1 and 3, https://www.ti.com/lit/ds/symlink/tps2553.pdf, read 2026-11-22) and the 0.15 mm E3_PICO_VSYS copper (0.224-0.248 A at +20 C on L2/L3, MODEL) never carries more than its rating; it recovers by itself when the fault clears (a -1 part could latch off on the start into the VSYS capacitance). EN tied to IN: on whenever LAB5 is present, like U553 in design/E5.json.; DBV SOT-23-6 per SLVS841G pin functions: 1 IN, 2 GND, 3 EN, 4 FAULT, 5 ILIM, 6 OUT. FAULT is an active-low open-drain output and is left unconnected (no input reads it; a VSYS fault shows as a Pico brown-out). IN takes the 0.1 uF ceramic C344 to GND as close to the IC as possible (pin function table).; Accept LCSC lots only with marking 2553 (parts.json U-TPS2553DBVR); never the latch-off -1 part here." (at 0 0 0) (effects (font (size 1.016 1.016)) (hide yes)))
